// Package servoimpl is the runtime that code written by `servo generate`
// calls, and that nothing else should. It is not for direct use: every
// exported identifier here exists to be named from a generated servo_gen.go,
// which lives in your package rather than servo's and can therefore only
// reach what is exported.
//
// It is exempt from servo's compatibility promise, the Versioning section
// of CHANGELOG.md. Signatures and behaviour here change in any release, in
// step with the generator that calls them, because a generated file is
// regenerated rather than edited and always calls the servoimpl of the
// servo version that wrote it. Putting these helpers in package servo would
// have frozen them as public API the moment a release shipped them, which
// is how RunStop, MergeNodeResults and LingerWindow came to be there: they
// remain, deprecated, for files generated before v3.5.0.
//
// The one exception is the ContractN constants. Each generated file names
// the contract it was written against, `const _ = servoimpl.Contract1`, so
// a file that needs a newer runtime than the go.mod pins fails to compile
// on that line, with a comment beside it naming the servo version it needs,
// instead of somewhere inside a helper whose signature moved. A constant is
// added when the generator starts relying on new runtime behaviour and is
// never removed within a major version, so a file generated by any v3
// release keeps compiling against every later one.
//
// servoimpl may import package servo, and does: the reports, node errors
// and budgets it works with are servo's public types. servo never imports
// servoimpl. Beyond servo it imports only the standard library, like the
// rest of the runtime.
package servoimpl
